WithUploads
  # order defined
  does not allow STI
  #uploads_cascade_deleted_on_destroy?
    when uploads_sharding_key is empty
      is expected to equal false
    when uploads_sharding_key contains namespace_id
      is expected to equal true
    when uploads_sharding_key contains project_id
      is expected to equal true
    when uploads_sharding_key contains only organization_id
      is expected to equal true
    when model does not respond to uploads_sharding_key
      is expected to equal false
  #capture_mounted_remote_uploaders
    when uploads_cascade_deleted_on_destroy? is false
      does not query uploads or register after_commit hook
    when uploads_cascade_deleted_on_destroy? is true
      when there are no uploads at all
        does not register an after_commit hook
      when there are only FILE_UPLOADERS uploads stored remotely
        does not capture them (they are handled by fast_destroy)
      when there are only local mounted uploads
        does not register an after_commit hook
      when there are remote mounted uploads with nil mount_point
        passes nil to retrieve_uploader
      when there are remote mounted uploads
        snapshots uploaders and schedules remote file deletion after commit
        tracks exceptions without re-raising when remote deletion fails
        does not delete when uploader file is nil
  #sweep_mounted_uploads
    when the file is already gone
      removes the upload row carrierwave left behind without deleting files
    when the file is still present
      leaves the cleanup to carrierwave
    when the upload is stored remotely and the object is gone
      removes the upload row without touching object storage
    when the model has no uploads
      does not schedule any file deletion
    when a model mounts several uploaders and only one file is gone
      sweeps the row carrierwave skipped and leaves the other file to carrierwave
    when the model also has a FileUploader upload
      leaves those rows to use_fast_destroy
    when the sharding key FK cascade-deletes the rows first
      leaves the cleanup to carrierwave
  before_destroy callback registration
    fires capture_mounted_remote_uploaders on destroy
    fires sweep_mounted_uploads on destroy
    registers capture_mounted_remote_uploaders before the fast_destroy callback
  after_commit callback order
    runs carrierwave cleanup before the after_commit queue
    Project
      runs the after_commit queue before carrierwave cleanup
  end-to-end destroy with remote mounted uploads
    deletes remote files after the model is destroyed
    when model has organization_id-only sharding key
      attempts remote file cleanup via capture_mounted_remote_uploaders
    when a model with organization_id sharding key and a mounted remote uploader is cascade-deleted via organization destroy
      does not delete remote files because DB cascade bypasses Rails callbacks
    when a model with organization_id sharding key is destroyed directly via Rails
      deletes remote files after the model is destroyed

